{"availability":"available","full":"DanTCIM/ValAct_RAG","name":"ValAct_RAG","description":"Retrieval Augmented Generation for Life Valuation Actuarial Documentations","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":12,"forks":4,"created":"2024-03-02T20:41:02Z","updated":"2026-10-05T20:54:26Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["actuary","streamlit"],"demo":"https://valact-search.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:55.598Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:55.598Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:55.598Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:55.598Z","stars":12,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project aims to create a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) process for actuaries to ask questions about a set of Life Valuation Actuarial documents. The RAG process utilizes the power of the large language model (LLM) to provide quick answers to questions about the documents.","However, RAG is not without challenges, i.e., hallucination and inaccuracy. The project allows verifiability by providing the context an LLM used to arrive at those answers. This process enables actuaries to validate the LLM's answers, empowering them to make informed decisions. By combining the capabilities of LLM with verifiability, this RAG process offers actuaries a robust tool to leverage LLM technology effectively and extract maximum value.","The current example uses an Anthropic Claude model with a long context window suitable for understanding lengthy actuarial documents and citing across multiple sources in a single answer. The specific Claude version is configured in valact/settings.py (ANTHROPICMODEL) and may be updated over time as newer releases become available."],"features":["Statutory Accounting Principles","Principle-Based Reserving","Cash Flow Testing and Asset Adequacy Testing","Actuarial Standards of Practice related to Life Insurance","Caym